            <ArticleTitle>Does Weight Impact Anidulafungin Pharmacokinetics?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1289-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s40262-016-0401-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bodyweight has been shown to influence anidulafungin exposure, but data from obese patients are lacking. We determined anidulafungin pharmacokinetics (100-mg single dose) in eight morbidly obese subjects (body mass index &gt;40 kg/m(2)). Anidulafungin exposure was on average 32.5 % lower compared with the general patient population, suggesting dose increases may be required in this population.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
